serid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25486-farast","name":"Farast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T23:46:02-07:00","id":1326900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1326881#post1326881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Tzimisce<br /> * Normal Sabbat Info<br /> * EVILL MYSTERIOUS NEW SABBAT info</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to see Tzimisce that are less of a one-note freak show. There are a lot of ways to go with the clan, but too often they are all too similar - you've met one T, you've met them all.<br /> <br /> And I hope to see some useful info on the Sabbat and the SI.<br /> <br /> And rules for creating powers, so I can more easily house-rule the old bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T23:52:56-07:00","id":1326904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1326900#post1326900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to see Tzimisce that are less of a one-note freak show. There are a lot of ways to go with the clan, but too often they are all too similar - you've met one T, you've met them all.<br /> <br /> And I hope to see some useful info on the Sabbat and the SI.<br /> <br /> And rules for creating powers, so I can more easily house-rule the old bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping that they give the Tzimice a small retool as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;A large number of Tzimisce have undergone a cleansing ritual provided by Dracula that renounces Kupala, the Eldest, and others. This has reconciled the Old Clan and the new with these Tzimsice being somewhat less insane as well as sadistic than before. These Tzimisce now call Viccisitude (or their version of it) Protean like the Gangrel.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T08:52:14-07:00","id":1326978,"title":"","content":"Well, I hope for an optional rule to decouple Touchstones/Convictions (going a little further than &quot;don't have them&quot;). Several houserules about that were proposed in these forums, but I feel a canon optional rule on those same lines would be far easier to bargain with an ST.<br /> <br /> Also, <b>IF </b>the intention it's to use Disciplines as something more akin to Mage Spheres (as was suggested by some), where combinations of the basic Disciplines allow experienced vampires to &quot;build&quot; different powers, it would be neat to have some real guidelines (perhaps even rules?) about creating combined discipline powers. This is important if players are supposed to play with this idea. STs can reign trough pure fiat, but players could use some guides<br /> <br /> Rules (optional or not) that give Elders part of their old power back. For instance, some have proposed here that Elders could have more than 5 Discipline powers (more than one power per level). That's very nice, but it's not RAW. Something RAW on these lines would be interesting.<br /> Perhaps Elders would be more appropiate for an ST book, but I think Elder rules (much like rules to generate Disciplines) are going to be more useful for <i>players </i>that want to engage in that power level than to STs that can always fiat arround stuff. So, idk, I can see it either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T10:10:00-07:00","id":1326995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Farast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see#post1326877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So given that Mophidius/Onyx Path are likely to be hard at work creating this book I would be interested in hearing what people want to see out of this book. I would like to focus this more on mechanical and role playing tools rather than fluff (metaplot, history etc. etc.) as this is likely to be the primary tool for helping new players to create characters.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The book is being written and developed by Modiphius, not OPP. Dawkins is working on it as a freelancer, though I don't know if any other usual OPP freelancers are working on it. The book is also probably pretty close to being done, as they're expecting Advance PDFs in December according to Modiphius' email.<br /> <br /> They have stated (or clarified in the case of some people's speculation) that the book is a companion, with rules that can be used in conjunction with and in place of rules in the core book, but it's not a replacement core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1326881#post1326881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Tzimisce<br /> * Normal Sabbat Info<br /> * EVILL MYSTERIOUS NEW SABBAT info</div> </div> </div> </div>We've already been told all 13 clans including Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> We've also been told by one of the Modiphius writers that the Sabbat info will maintain the 'shrouded in mystery' angle, and that Sabbat written-as-PC-options will be relegated to an eventual Sabbat book. The 13 clans in the book will be written in the way they fit into the currently-playable sects.<br /> <br /> They did a couple of impromptu AMAs on the WoD5 Discord where we got this info.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1326900#post1326900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to see Tzimisce that are less of a one-note freak show. There are a lot of ways to go with the clan, but too often they are all too similar - you've met one T, you've met them all.<br /> <br /> And I hope to see some useful info on the Sabbat and the SI.<br /> <br /> And rules for creating powers, so I can more easily house-rule the old bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've said we'll get a 'state of the Sabbat' bit, but further clarified it'll be in the same vein of 'dark and mysterious and non-playable' as the core book, that the Tzimisce will be in the book and their powers will be 're-imagined' to fit the V5 style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1326900#post1326900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to see Tzimisce that are less of a one-note freak show. There are a lot of ways to go with the clan, but too often they are all too similar - you've met one T, you've met them all.<br /> <br /> And I hope to see some useful info on the Sabbat and the SI.<br /> <br /> And rules for creating powers, so I can more easily house-rule the old bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>They stated in the AMA there would be no alternate morality rules in the book.<br /> <br /> When I'm home and can copy/paste from Discord I can dump those quotes in here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T10:26:01-07:00","id":1327004,"title":"","content":"Thank you. That would be most helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T17:42:43-07:00","id":1327095,"title":"","content":"So here are the things we got from the impromptu AMA. Note that this is just the compiled answers.<br /> <br /> We had a few impromptu AMA's on the server a while ago, and both Matthew Dawkins and Khaldoun Khelil answered some questions regarding the upcoming V5 books. Here's a tl;dr of what we learned! <br /> <br /> From Matthew Dawkins:<br /> <br /> The PG will have Amalgams and alternate powers for Disciplines. Apparently 'Warlocks of all stripes will have some new toys to play with' but without context (hopefully more Rituals and BS powers).<br /> <br /> The Hecata section will talk about the Giovanni as they are linked to the Hecata; the Hecata section will not talk about the non-Hecata Giovanni. The non-Hecata Giovanni will be more covered in Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> Ravnos and Tzimisce will be in the PG.<br /> <br /> There will be info about the current state of the Sabbat in the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> It will not do mechanical rollbacks.<br /> <br /> Per Jason Carl on Twitch during the last LAbN it'll have new Merits, Flaws and Backgrounds as well as Discipline powers.<br /> <br /> From Khaldoun Khelil:<br /> <br /> The PG will be a supplement to the core rulebook - there will be material that can be used instead of the material in the corebook, but it's not intended to replace the corebook.<br /> <br /> All 13 Clans will be represented in the PG. Cults of the Blood Gods handles how bloodlines will be represented (Matthew Dawkins and his team found an elegant solution to them) and the content in the PG will follow this example.<br /> <br /> Both the Ravnos and the Tzimisce and their iconic abilites will be in the PG and they will be re-imagined to some degree to fit the V5 playstyle. Especially the Ravnos' core identity will be less racial/cultural and their powers will have a different source and methodology.<br /> <br /> Tha PG will include a lot of new Merits and powers.<br /> <br /> The PG will continue on the design decision to shroud the Sabbat in mystery and misinformation and will focus on the currently playable Sects and how the 13 Clans fit into them.<br /> <br /> There will be no alternative morality systems in the PG; V5 focuses on younger Kindred more unaware of Clan/Sect traditions and the V5 Humanity system is very modular as is and can be modified to fit very different moral codes that can approximate some paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T20:45:14-07:00","id":1327125,"title":"","content":"How do the elder arrange to establish themselves in an already elder territory as the Ashirra is.<br /> <br /> There are countless facts from this sect within Veil of Night, Iberia by Night, Dark Ages Europe, and most ignored/rewritten by V20 Dark Ages Vampire. Why create a (pop gullible sect as the &quot;drowed legacies&quot; when they were never mentioned before in any 1st ed/2nd ed/revised before, but applied in V20 (which has been to be CANON AGNOSTIC)? Kalku &quot;Tremere&quot; Prince taking over Buenos Aires seems like lazy writing to me, when Clanbook Toreador's Prince Alexandra and VtES card making her in the Inner Circle of the Camarilla is just ignoring the facts.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T21:00:21-07:00","id":1327128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1327125#post1327125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the elder arrange to establish themselves in an already elder territory as the Ashirra is.<br /> <br /> There are countless facts from this sect within Veil of Night, Iberia by Night, Dark Ages Europe, and most ignored/rewritten by V20 Dark Ages Vampire. Why create a (pop gullible sect as the &quot;drowed legacies&quot; when they were never mentioned before in any 1st ed/2nd ed/revised before, but applied in V20 (which has been to be CANON AGNOSTIC)? Kalku &quot;Tremere&quot; Prince taking over Buenos Aires seems like lazy writing to me, when Clanbook Toreador's Prince Alexandra and VtES card making her in the Inner Circle of the Camarilla is just ignoring the facts.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it possible she was Beckoned?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T15:08:44-07:00","id":1327273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1327095#post1327095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravnos and Tzimisce will be in the PG.<br /> The PG (...) will focus on the currently playable Sects and how the 13 Clans fit into them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually quite interesting. And if &quot;half the Tzimisce&quot; takes the Anarchs' side, as per the Lasombra with the Camarilla, it adds a new rivalry between two clans who have been allies and the bastions of the Sabbat for almost a millenium. Also, I can see the Ravnos spliting between the two Sects under &quot;normal circumstances, but they probably can't afford a split right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1327095#post1327095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cults of the Blood Gods handles how bloodlines will be represented (Matthew Dawkins and his team found an elegant solution to them)</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the term &quot;elegant solution&quot; concerning the bloodlines. Let's see how it plays out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1327095#post1327095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There will be no alternative morality systems in the PG; (...) the V5 Humanity system is very modular as is and can be modified to fit very different moral codes that can approximate some paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a hint that even a &quot;Full Path System&quot; will use the Convictions systems?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25354-madcello","name":"Madcello","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T15:47:06-07:00","id":1327286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1326904#post1326904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm hoping that they give the Tzimice a small retool as well.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;A large number of Tzimisce have undergone a cleansing ritual provided by Dracula that renounces Kupala, the Eldest, and others. This has reconciled the Old Clan and the new with these Tzimsice being somewhat less insane as well as sadistic than before. These Tzimisce now call Viccisitude (or their version of it) Protean like the Gangrel.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Reintroduction of Byzantine era worship of Gesu and the Dracon would be a good development for more cerebral Tzimisce","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24869-zorin001","name":"Zorin001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T17:27:25-07:00","id":1327298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1327128#post1327128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it possible she was Beckoned?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really doubt that she wasn't. She is Inner Circle of the Camarilla and Inconnu, she probably is more important than Hardestadt IMO.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T19:11:19-07:00","id":1327332,"title":"","content":"An in setitng reason for the changes (Hunger/reduced stats/change of disciplines) or explanation of how fluff in the history of the game was possible if not supported by the new system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T19:55:38-07:00","id":1327342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madcello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1327273#post1327273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a hint that even a &quot;Full Path System&quot; will use the Convictions systems?</div> </div> </div> </div>We will see when we get there. Dawkins did mention today during the Twitch cast that he's not sure that the original thoughts of Sabbat methods for Convictions/Touchstones he talked about in the Gentleman Gamer videos will still be applicable. Honestly, as Khalil said, you can do just about anything with Convictions/Touchstones you could with Paths. Not 100%, but pretty close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T19:56:42-07:00","id":1327343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1327332#post1327332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An in setitng reason for the changes (Hunger/reduced stats/change of disciplines) or explanation of how fluff in the history of the game was possible if not supported by the new system?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Odd question for the PG thread, but no. It's just treated as how some of this stuff always has been. Considering all the Level 5 Disciplines now used to be Elder Powers, it's just 'scaling' rather than removal of anything anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T12:25:15-07:00","id":1327631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1326904#post1326904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm hoping that they give the Tzimice a small retool as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;A large number of Tzimisce have undergone a cleansing ritual provided by Dracula that renounces Kupala, the Eldest, and others. This has reconciled the Old Clan and the new with these Tzimsice being somewhat less insane as well as sadistic than before. These Tzimisce now call Viccisitude (or their version of it) Protean like the Gangrel.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I barely makes sense that Dracula had the ability to enact a ritual that affects the whole clan (he had Koldunic Sorcery 5 in Children of the Night). Though I understand in a symbolic level him being the one to create it. But let's not forget that the ritual made to destroy the blood bonds used magics from Velya (who had Koldunic Sorcery 8 and if we reverse his disciplines, his embrace would be around 100 BC), Lugoj (who is statistically unknown) and Lambach Ruthven (who is claimed to be around before most organized religions, therefore, probably older than Velya).<br /> <br /> Here's a small list that are more appropriate for it:<br /> . The Dracon<br /> . Kartarirya<br /> . Demdemeh<br /> . Ionache<br /> . Ruthven (probably Lambach)<br /> . &quot;Keeper of the Faith&quot;<br /> . Danika Ruthven<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 07-26-2019, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T13:24:26-07:00","id":1327645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1327631#post1327631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I barely makes sense that Dracula had the ability to enact a ritual that affects the whole clan (he had Koldunic Sorcery 5 in Children of the Night). Though I understand in a symbolic level him being the one to create it. But let's not forget that the ritual made to destroy the blood bonds used magics from Velya (who had Koldunic Sorcery 8 and if we reverse his disciplines, his embrace would be around 100 BC), Lugoj (who is statistically unknown) and Lambach Ruthven (who is claimed to be around before most organized religions, therefore, probably older than Velya).<br /> <br /> Here's a small list that are more appropriate for it:<br /> . The Dracon<br /> . Kartarirya<br /> . Demdemeh<br /> . Ionache<br /> . Ruthven (probably Lambach)<br /> . &quot;Keeper of the Faith&quot;<br /> . Danika Ruthven<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed the ritual would be done individually to those Tzimisce who want to perform it.<br /> -Completely Missing the Point<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T11:08:25-07:00","id":1328329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1327095#post1327095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here are the things we got from the impromptu AMA. Note that this is just the compiled answers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There will be info about the current state of the Sabbat in the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> It will not do mechanical rollbacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The PG will be a supplement to the core rulebook - there will be material that can be used instead of the material in the corebook, but it's not intended to replace the corebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Both the Ravnos and the Tzimisce and their iconic abilites will be in the PG and they will be re-imagined to some degree to fit the V5 playstyle. Especially the Ravnos' core identity will be less racial/cultural and their powers will have a different source and methodology.<br /> <br /> <br /> The PG will continue on the design decision to shroud the Sabbat in mystery and misinformation and will focus on the currently playable Sects and how the 13 Clans fit into them.<br /> <br /> <br /> There will be no alternative morality systems in the PG; V5 focuses on younger Kindred more unaware of Clan/Sect traditions and the V5 Humanity system is very modular as is and can be modified to fit very different moral codes that can approximate some paths.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aaaand there went my remaining interest out the window.<br /> <br /> Clearly, they want to go in a particular direction with this game and not really want to at least make some concessions and optional rules for the folks who had the talked-to-death misgivings with V5, like me. That's fine, I wish everyone who enjoys this edition happy gaming. For me, I'll remain with the 20ths until V6, then, we'll see, but V5 is just not my cup of tea and I don't see any real chances for that to change.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-31-2019, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T14:21:28-07:00","id":1328378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1328329#post1328329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Aaaand there went my remaining interest out the window.<br /> <br /> Clearly, they want to go in a particular direction with this game and not really want to at least make some concessions and optional rules to the folks who had the talked-to-death misgivings with V5, like me. That's fine, I wish everyone who enjoys this edition happy gaming. For me, I'll remain with the 20ths until V6, then, we'll see, but V5 is just not my cup of tea and I don't see any real chances for that to change.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please explain the reason for your statement?<br /> I was interested in the premise of rules that allow other rules to be viable for the player ... as old disciplines so that players can play controlling real vampires again; Do you think this fits in &quot;using rules other than the main book&quot;? Can I be cautiously hopeful? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T07:31:45-07:00","id":1330744,"title":"","content":"I somehow think that we are gonna get the Old Clan Tzimisce in the Players Guide, its what they have been calling it in the V5 books, which means Vicissitude might not be in the book yet (I might be wrong of course), but it is probable that the Fiends in the PGB will be the non-Sabbat remnants, which is exactly the concept of the Old Clan Tzimisce faction. I really don't care that much for having Vicissitude right now as a written Discipline (or power/amalgam of Protean), I'm more interested in being able to play the Noble/Rebel and Fiendish/Macabre Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Also, more Advantages and Flaws? Please do, I love the way they have done it in V5, although some of the most simple Merits and Flaws have been only listed contextualized in Loresheets (things like Clan merits or flaws, character background bonuses....), I really would like even more options. The V3-V20 Merits and Flaws got crazy long, redundant and out there, V5 way of making is much more elegant and streamlined. Can't wait to see what they will have.<br /> <br /> I always liked the idea of the Clan of Rogues and Mystics in the Ravnos, but the execution was always terrible, I don't remember any interesting or important Ravnos character in the canon, and people always looked only at their Discipline instead of the Clan itself. Removing it from the Gypsies and Indian mold will be a healthy improvement that will add one more interesting Clan to explore in the game. [If you can't tell I really liked what they've done with the Setites, Banu Haqim and seem to be doing with the Giovanni; linking an entire Clan to a single unique culture is a gimmick and limits the scope, besides, the 13 Clans are supposed to be global, Bloodlines are more of a local thing].<br /> <br /> I think talking with the Storyteller and determining the right Convictions (and maybe homebrew a different Touchstone that its not a mortal but a concept or ritual followed perhaps) and adding some Loresheets for the different Roads, is the way to do Paths in V5. And although I love some concepts of the Paths there's many who used it for a cheap way out of repercussion, and everyone that gnarled at Humanity as a boring or limited Path probably didn't get the original idea of the game very well. <br /> <br /> V5 seems very well done mechanically and adding more tools to the box seems great, because the game has depth, it just needs more options.<br /> <br /> At last, I'm interested to see more Alchemy formulas, more Blood Sorcery (how are they gonna do the paths? rituals? weird amalgam? independent and less limited powers by level?), Oblivion rituals (Necromancy can't lose its touch baby) and more powers can only be a good thing for the Disciplines -which by the way had some levels that only have &quot;Draught of&quot;, which is kinda bullshrimp for some vampires- and can be very imaginative if done right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T11:14:18-07:00","id":1331091,"title":"","content":"\u201cI really don't care that much for having Vicissitude right now as a written Discipline (or power/amalgam of Protean)\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t see a feasible way to combine (Fleshcraft?) Protean and Vicissitude in any satisfactory fashion, anyway. Not if you\u2019re a fan of both Disciplines, that is. It will be too drastic a case of choosing either/or, with the end result being much less than the sum of its parts. <br /> <br /> Unless it\u2019s something where Protean can become a system similar to Oblivion, with Protean being the main Discipline and \u201cVicissitude\u201d dealing more with fleshcrafting/metamorphic rituals stemming from it. Sounds weird when I type it out loud, I admit, but that would allow for both the horrific fleshcrafting we love as well as the traditional Protean shapeshifting, while also somewhat reflecting Fiend mysticism. <br /> <br /> I am very curious to see how they attempt to mix them together, though. Can\u2019t wait for the PG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T11:32:09-07:00","id":1331094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1331091#post1331091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very curious to see how they attempt to mix them together, though. Can\u2019t wait for the PG.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were to do it, I would combine the first 3 levels of Vicissitude on a single 3rd level Amalgam or a higher level power. This isn't hard because these powers were one the extension of the other, and could be defined as &quot;altering flesh and bone in a very free form way&quot;. Higher level powers are mostly alternate forms for the vampire. They could be rituals or specialized Protean transmutations.<br /> <br /> The obvious Discipline to combine with Protean to create Vicissitude as an Amalgam it's Blood Magic (they have a theme of body control, and there's an aestheticall link between flesh and blood since they're most oftend found together), sadly I don't think they are going to have it because their other two classic Disciplines exist. Albeit it would make sense if they did, Tzimisce are as known for their blood magicians as the Assamites. I think it would be thematically the best choice, and not the most controversial change of V5 by a long shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-15-2019, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T12:08:24-07:00","id":1331097,"title":"","content":"The issue I have with the Amalgam powers is that it's far too easy to make the iconic aspects of the clan inaccessible. Both Malkavians and Lasombra are big examples of this. If you want to be a Lasombra and use the iconic Lasombra power of Arms of Ahriman, then your only build is Obtenebration 2 Protean 2 and you are either an Alley Cat or a Scene Queen. Malkavians have it better with the Predatory Type choices (because there are predators for both Obfuscate and Dominate), but you are still locked into a One True Build.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you <i>don't</i> have Vicissitude, then what's the point of having the Tzimisce as a distinct clan? No one in the history of ever cared about the gimpy Ventrue that are the Old Clan Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T14:11:38-07:00","id":1331112,"title":"","content":"I'm really inclined to think in a similar vein as to what was described above. Many mentions of the Tzimisce in the existing books also make reference to the &quot;Old Clan&quot; which leads me to believe we'll see something come up in V5 metaplot (likely the PG since it will introduce the Clan) that talks about how the Old Clan Tzimisce have been making a recent resurgence, are Embracing new Childer (opening up options for standard characters and not just Elders - this may well have something to do with the Beckoning starting to lure the Old Clan Elders away). This will be our standard Tzimisce for the time being (as bringing them to the fore would leave options for them to potentially try and side with the Camarilla, Anarchs, or continue to run somewhat Independent).<br /> <br /> The twisted fleshcrafters of the old editions core Clan, the ones with Vicissitude, I'm starting to think are going to be saved for the later coming Sabbat deep dive so we can use them as the monsters of our games. I'm honestly strongly inclined to believe they are going to lean on Vicissitude itself having corrupted much of the core Clan into puppets of the Antediluvian. This would position the twisted Discipline that is Vicissitude as the signature power of the &quot;creepy monsters&quot; Sect that the Sabbat is going to be positioned into. It will still feature other Clans of course, as the classic Antitribu versions (including any remaining Lasombra being tagged that at this point). So they get a creepy power to accompany their creepy persona and will be left more to the realm of STs as opposed to players (though I suspect we will get details on how to play the Sabbat still in a potential Sabbat book, people want to do it and it would be crazy for the brand not to exploit that desire from a business standpoint). But the inherent intent will be that these are the antagonists of your worlds (outside of the other more standard Camarilla v Anarch that V5 leans into). I could even see them lean into the Vicissitude infection for this as well, or at least adapting the concept into it being more a tool of the Ante.<br /> <br /> At least, that remains my hot take on the Tzimisce to this day. I called that a while back, actually, in another thread in general passing. So far none of the released content has made me think any differently from this either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">-Red</span></b> V5 Fan Content: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1259556-v5-the-masquerade\" target=\"_blank\">The Masquerade</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256114-v5-tzimisce-and-vicissitude\" target=\"_blank\">Tzimisce and Vicissitude</a> (non Program take), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1253331-loresheets-chicago\" target=\"_blank\">Loresheet: Chicago</a> (pre CbN V5), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1251576-v5-resonance-flavor\" target=\"_blank\">Resonance Flavor</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1291918-v5-morality\" target=\"_blank\">Morality System</a> Project Manager, Developer, Community Outreach at <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Entertainment</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6164-red-eye","name":"Red Eye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6164_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T14:12:13-07:00","id":1331113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1331097#post1331097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue I have with the Amalgam powers is that it's far too easy to make the iconic aspects of the clan inaccessible. Both Malkavians and Lasombra are big examples of this. If you want to be a Lasombra and use the iconic Lasombra power of Arms of Ahriman, then your only build is Obtenebration 2 Protean 2 and you are either an Alley Cat or a Scene Queen. Malkavians have it better with the Predatory Type choices (because there are predators for both Obfuscate and Dominate), but you are still locked into a One True Build.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you <i>don't</i> have Vicissitude, then what's the point of having the Tzimisce as a distinct clan? No one in the history of ever cared about the gimpy Ventrue that are the Old Clan Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Inaccessible at chargen&quot; doesn't mean &quot;not accessible at all&quot;. Gangrel are known for turning into bats, but you can't do that at character creation either.<br /> <br /> Imo, if a clan ceases to be playable if you can't have one specific power at chargen, then that was a gimmick, not a clan. There's more to the Lasombra than shadow tentacles, and more to the Malkavians than making people go insane. Similarly, imo, there should be more to the Tzimisce than body horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T15:24:18-07:00","id":1331126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1331113#post1331113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gangrel are known for turning into bats, but you can't do that at character creation either.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T17:49:05-07:00","id":1331140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red Eye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1331112#post1331112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least, that remains my hot take on the Tzimisce to this day. I called that a while back, actually, in another thread in general passing. So far none of the released content has made me think any differently from this either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, more or less. But I think Vicissitude might become one of those dangerous powers that PCs may still use, but one which gradually destroys them. That is it functionally becomes an infernal taint. Yes, you can use it to disguise yourself, heal a wound, or pull someone's face off. But every such use give you some kind of corruption score which is very difficult to get rid of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T18:03:53-07:00","id":1331141,"title":"","content":"I think it'll probably just be an alternate power of Protean and probably less powerful.<br /> <br /> Though I wouldn't be surprised if it's a Blood Sorcery/Protean Power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T19:15:03-07:00","id":1331150,"title":"","content":"I don't as much like what I'm hearing, vis a vis the sharp categorization of Vicissitude as all bad, all the time. And the idea that if the Tzimisce are going to be player options, that they cannot have Vicissitude. Yes, Sabbat Tzimisce tend to go way overboard with it, but I still think there's a middle ground between All Vicissitude and No Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> For one thing, I rankle at the very idea of depriving players of choices, all else being equal. For another, labeling the Discipline that allows a vampire to tailor their body to their desires as Always Evil has some...unfortunate implications. This is a problem going back to the start of VtM, of course, because it unfairly demonizes what, say, Transexuals/Transgender or Transhumanists believe or wish. I'd think that, with the benefit of hindsight and a reexamination of values, we'd use the shifts in editions as a chance to embrace Vicissitude's positive benefits, as well as its capacity to produce total monsters.<br /> <br /> (Don't misunderstand me to mean I think there shouldn't be Tzimisce monsters, don't be silly. Their utility as antagonists is simply unmatched, especially in more action-oriented games. I just think there ought to be less villainous, morally neutral Tzimisce, for whom Vicissitude is liberating in a non-horrific way).<br /> <br /> If you're going to change the &quot;meta&quot;, as it were, I'd prefer to establish Anarch Tzimisce as the aforementioned middle ground between All Vicissitude (the Sabbat) and No Vicissitude (the Old Clan). Tzimisce who embrace the utility of the Discipline, but don't &quot;start a religion over it&quot;, as it were (though that ship sailed centuries ago). Their alterations are subtle, because they care both about blending in and maintaining a semblance of Humanity. They don't turn people into furniture; at worst, they seal a person's mouth shut when it's convenient (they ARE still vampires, after all, even in the Anarchs). It would be fascinating, indeed, for books to establish how the culture of each part of Clan Tzimisce differs when it comes to their signature Discipline. A sort of &quot;spectrum of fleshcrafting&quot;, with the Sabbat and Old Clan being at opposite ends, and everything in between. How the unique powers afforded by Vicissitude present endless and creative temptations for relatively humane Kindred, and the slippery slope that arises from embracing its visceral gifts.<br /> <br /> I've also got an idea for a couple Combination Discipline powers that might assist the &quot;weekend fleshcrafter&quot;, that involve a greater emphasis on temporary transformations. I'll probably make a [V20] thread about it. Suffice to say, though, that it would be more on-brand for Anarch Tzimisce to cultivate a capacity for Vicissitude whose benefits could be turned on and off. That way, they don't have to <i>unlive</i> with their modifications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T19:38:24-07:00","id":1331155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1331150#post1331150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't as much like what I'm hearing, vis a vis the sharp categorization of Vicissitude as all bad, all the time. And the idea that if the Tzimisce are going to be player options, that they cannot have Vicissitude. Yes, Sabbat Tzimisce tend to go way overboard with it, but I still think there's a middle ground between All Vicissitude and No Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> For one thing, I rankle at the very idea of depriving players of choices, all else being equal. For another, labeling the Discipline that allows a vampire to tailor their body to their desires as Always Evil has some...unfortunate implications. This is a problem going back to the start of VtM, of course, because it unfairly demonizes what, say, Transexuals/Transgender or Transhumanists believe or wish. I'd think that, with the benefit of hindsight and a reexamination of values, we'd use the shifts in editions as a chance to embrace Vicissitude's positive benefits, as well as its capacity to produce total monsters.<br /> <br /> (Don't misunderstand me to mean I think there shouldn't be Tzimisce monsters, don't be silly. Their utility as antagonists is simply unmatched, especially in more action-oriented games. I just think there ought to be less villainous, morally neutral Tzimisce, for whom Vicissitude is liberating in a non-horrific way).<br /> <br /> If you're going to change the &quot;meta&quot;, as it were, I'd prefer to establish Anarch Tzimisce as the aforementioned middle ground between All Vicissitude (the Sabbat) and No Vicissitude (the Old Clan). Tzimisce who embrace the utility of the Discipline, but don't &quot;start a religion over it&quot;, as it were (though that ship sailed centuries ago). Their alterations are subtle, because they care both about blending in and maintaining a semblance of Humanity. They don't turn people into furniture; at worst, they seal a person's mouth shut when it's convenient (they ARE still vampires, after all, even in the Anarchs). It would be fascinating, indeed, for books to establish how the culture of each part of Clan Tzimisce differs when it comes to their signature Discipline. A sort of &quot;spectrum of fleshcrafting&quot;, with the Sabbat and Old Clan being at opposite ends, and everything in between. How the unique powers afforded by Vicissitude present endless and creative temptations for relatively humane Kindred, and the slippery slope that arises from embracing its visceral gifts.<br /> <br /> I've also got an idea for a couple Combination Discipline powers that might assist the &quot;weekend fleshcrafter&quot;, that involve a greater emphasis on temporary transformations. I'll probably make a [V20] thread about it. Suffice to say, though, that it would be more on-brand for Anarch Tzimisce to cultivate a capacity for Vicissitude whose benefits could be turned on and off. That way, they don't have to <i>unlive</i> with their modifications.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's why Vicissitude is being split from Protean. Mind you, White Wolf has held to &quot;Vicissitude=Bad&quot; and &quot;Protean=Fine&quot; for literally 25 years. Even when they got rid of the Soul Eaters, they just made Vicissitude bad because of Kupala and the Eldest.<br /> <br /> I don't know why it's always evil but they've doubled, tripled, and quadrupled down on it always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T20:16:53-07:00","id":1331158,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Vicissitude is probably the oddest discipline. It is also probably the one least connected to either the folklore of vampire or most horror depictions of the undead. It leans in mostly to Lumley's &quot;Necroscope&quot; series and to a smaller degree the Tzimisce mimic the <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Cenobites </span></span>of Barker's &quot;Hellraiser.&quot; They are odd creatures and it is an odd power. It also lends itself the least to &quot;Captain Vampire&quot; type of play.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 08-15-2019, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-16T17:40:16-07:00","id":1331262,"title":"","content":"I would like to see the return of six dots powers.<br /> I know that they are trying to &quot;power down&quot; the setting, so to speak, but getting rid of the majority of Elders should be enough to accomplish that. There's no need to drastically weaken the ones who remain Like Helena or Critias in V5 Chicago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-16T18:57:01-07:00","id":1331274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1331262#post1331262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see the return of six dots powers.<br /> I know that they are trying to &quot;power down&quot; the setting, so to speak, but getting rid of the majority of Elders should be enough to accomplish that. There's no need to drastically weaken the ones who remain Like Helena or Critias in V5 Chicago.</div> </div> </div> </div>In-universe: I think they stated in Chicago by Night that those who resist the Beckoning feel weaker.<br /> <br /> Out of universe: The power levels of Level 5 powers are usually consistent with Level 6 powers now so actually vampires have gotten stronger in many cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T05:39:23-07:00","id":1331327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1331274#post1331274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In-universe: I think they stated in Chicago by Night that those who resist the Beckoning feel weaker.<br /> <br /> Out of universe: The power levels of Level 5 powers are usually consistent with Level 6 powers now so actually vampires have gotten stronger in many cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Giving Level 5 unique powers is all well and good but that's also symptomatic of this edition trying to bridge the gap between Elders and the PCs that players tend to make. Vampires who had Skills and Attributes above 5 have been severely weakened.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T06:12:36-07:00","id":1331328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1331327#post1331327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Giving Level 5 unique powers is all well and good but that's also symptomatic of this edition trying to bridge the gap between Elders and the PCs that players tend to make. Vampires who had Skills and Attributes above 5 have been severely weakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a good argument they were severely overpowered.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T17:23:12-07:00","id":1331406,"title":"","content":"In hindsight, it\u2019s kind of amazing that there isn\u2019t a Tzimsce vampire or a Revenant family line known for being brilliant surgeons and healers. Vicissitude literally has no healing powers at all, in any edition of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T17:30:44-07:00","id":1331407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1331406#post1331406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In hindsight, it\u2019s kind of amazing that there isn\u2019t a Tzimsce vampire or a Revenant family line known for being brilliant surgeons and healers. Vicissitude literally has no healing powers at all, in any edition of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would contradict the fact that, again, every edition of the game has doubled down on what monstrous evil alien bastards the Tzimisce are.<br /> <br /> Even when Souleaters stopped being a thing.<br /> <br /> Then it was, &quot;Tainted by the Eldest!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Tainted by Kupala!&quot;<br /> <br /> Tainted by EVILLLL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T19:12:57-07:00","id":1331430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1331328#post1331328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a good argument they were severely overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fundamentally disagree with that tough I would be interested to hear why you think they were overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-25T20:18:20-07:00","id":1332598,"title":"","content":"I don't really understand the discussion between Vicissitude being good or bad, specially because Blood Sorcery is mostly cruel as heel and Dominate can be nasty in more ways than a gross Viciss. use can be. Either way. The simplest solution, in tandem with V5 design choices so far, would be making Rituals for Protean as stated before. I think Vicissitude just isn't so diverse in its levels that would warrant a unique Discipline power tree. Quietus had the same thing with mashing weird things together or being redundant in some versions, specially higher than level five powers. Anyhow, I believe that twisting people up (against their wishes) should warrant Taints.<br /> <br /> But enough with that. I'm excited for the new systems and mechanics they are working on, the ones that do not revamp the originals but can be used instead and et cetera. I really liked the small but workable systems they've put in the Camarilla and Anarch books (though the latter was as mechanic). What you people think they will be about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T20:13:48-07:00","id":1332769,"title":"","content":"The Ravnos actually seem pretty easy to fix. WIth their numbers dwindled down after the week of nightmares, they have to go through heavy mass embracing over 20 years and can't be ethnically picky. The result is a clan that is much more diverse ethnically while also still keeping the core rogues and mystics theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T02:42:55-07:00","id":1332794,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me what they say so far.<br /> <br /> New Merits and especially new Flaws are something I'm looking forward to, interesting Flaws are always fun.<br /> <br /> I hope they stick to the more thematic BLOOD magic theme for new warlock powers, I like that a lot more.<br /> <br /> Ravnos, decoupling them from a specific culture is probably best. Although I think I liked the Indian Ravnos they came up with after nuking them^^ (never used them so not 100% sure). So I hope they'll orient them more towards them and not so much the gypsy tricksters type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","user":"nobby","date":". 08-27-2019, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T09:35:46-07:00","id":1332990,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to see some info on how the modern night vampires view or interact with the other major denizens of the World of Darkness, especially the Werewolves and Mages, but also Changelings and Wraiths (though I'm guessing well see some of that in the Hecata section of Cults of the Blood Gods).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-28T11:10:34-07:00","id":1333000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1332990#post1332990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like to see some info on how the modern night vampires view or interact with the other major denizens of the World of Darkness, especially the Werewolves and Mages, but also Changelings and Wraiths (though I'm guessing well see some of that in the Hecata section of Cults of the Blood Gods).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good request. The classic WoD always had the feature of the splats not working well together. Some shifts could make them easier to use together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T19:28:09-07:00","id":1333918,"title":"","content":"I really liked the way CoD did it, Mage the Awakening seemed really prepared to it. But I also love the CoD games and scenarios so I'm biased.<br /> Which makes me wonder how the Storyteller 5th edition will do with the other games, I think the Hunger system will work awesomely in their way with Rage, Paradox, Angst.... <br /> But back to topic, I hope more Convictions, Merits and Flaws and more generic and usable Loresheets show up in the Players Handbook. They are all great systems, just need more options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T08:20:09-07:00","id":1333955,"title":"","content":"I would like to see more Photographs like in the Core Rulebook as art. I wont say it was all good but the Brujah headshot and Ventrue photos really stand out for me. I would like to see the photos portray a greater diversity of each clans themes though. I am pretty sure not all Brujah wear leather, ripped jeans and have tatts. <br /> <br /> I realize I may be in a minority here on this one but some of the photos were really great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T10:15:13-07:00","id":1335544,"title":"","content":"I would like to see more Photographs too. Though IMHO the ones for the Nosferatu were way too pretty. It was nice seeing some women Nos though. I would like to see the Photos/artwork line up better with the Clan Flaw.<br /> <br /> More example Convictions and esp Touchstones would be great.<br /> <br /> Any Idea of what book will include Necromancy? and how it will be handled. ie Will they merge it with Blood Sorcery? or something more akin to previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25631-tashag","name":"TashaG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T10:41:52-07:00","id":1335551,"title":"","content":"Necromancy will be merged with Oblivion, and will show up in both the Player's Guide and Cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T14:38:42-08:00","id":1364849,"title":"","content":"I always forget, but more Predator types would be cool too.<br /> And I really hope the 13 Clans are well developed and described in this book, with Loresheets (for each) and Advantages that expand upon what we have. I still think the Ministry is really bad explained in V5 Anarchs, you just don't get to see what they are doing exactly and what they are now. Cult of the Blood Gods did it way better funny enough. So I hope a good and inspiring text to the Clans.<br /> (I also think we might not get Vicissitude just yet, might get the Old Clan Tzimisce instead, which if fine by my, I like Tzimisce RP better than their powers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T14:52:35-08:00","id":1364853,"title":"","content":"I really hope we get Vicissitude. I really do. I have a number of character ideas for the Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 02-02-2020, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T15:32:48-08:00","id":1364860,"title":"","content":"I also hope we get something on the Tzimisce and Vicissitude, but apparently its on the bubble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T17:06:21-08:00","id":1364876,"title":"","content":"Sounds like I'm going to have to houserule the hell out of the Tzims to give them that Wamphyri flavor I crave from the clan. Slightly frustrating, but ultimately fine. I've always had to houserule them to a substantial degree anyway, since they were somewhat close to the Wamphyri, but not nearly close enough for my liking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T18:12:22-08:00","id":1364889,"title":"","content":"Some great ideas on this thread, I have to say! <br /> <br /> I think that there has to be the full quotient of 13 Clans in this book really, and I would like to see how the Disciplines could be developed and expanded a bit. Basically, any of the crunch, including alternative character generation and experience tracks should be done in this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T18:15:47-08:00","id":1364890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1364889#post1364889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some great ideas on this thread, I have to say! <br /> <br /> I think that there has to be the full quotient of 13 Clans in this book really, and I would like to see how the Disciplines could be developed and expanded a bit. Basically, any of the crunch, including alternative character generation and experience tracks should be done in this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean with alternative character generation? Genuine question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T19:32:48-08:00","id":1364906,"title":"","content":"We do know that the Players Guide is finished....but that they rejected the Ravnos and Tzimisce sections, sending them back for re-writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T19:58:43-08:00","id":1364912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1364890#post1364890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean with alternative character generation? Genuine question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Faster generation, mainly for NPCs but a character generation system that doesn\u2019t require a full session of play. Archetypal templates even - and these were included for each Clan in the original 1st edition Players Guide. You could also include rules for generating older vampires, either by Generation or just by timeline. I like the idea of doing some sort of life path generator that could stretch back to antiquity. Other random tables could also be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T23:05:54-08:00","id":1365180,"title":"","content":"I think in the NPC department V5 is fine, great even, we already got beasts, humans and monsters. And I specially like how they are handling stats, the low-level NPCs now have just a basic pool dice and exceptional ones, which is exactly what I want when seeing what I'l roll for them during a game, and even the full-fledged NPCs got some treatment to be more readable too, like the 'worse pool die' / 'best pool die' numbers we got in Chicago by Night or Cult of the Blood Gods NPCs I think.<br /> More character options, relevant and interesting information (setting, plot, gameplay/roleplay, character, storytelling) are what I trully want to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T09:27:19-08:00","id":1365277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1364906#post1364906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do know that the Players Guide is finished....but that they rejected the Ravnos and Tzimisce sections, sending them back for re-writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my interest in it has dropped. Most of the rest of the book seem nice enough but not essential. Without the Ravnos and Tzimisce I do not see a need to buy the book.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T10:19:52-08:00","id":1365291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1365277#post1365277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, my interest in it has dropped. Most of the rest of the book seem nice enough but not essential. Without the Ravnos and Tzimisce I do not see a need to buy the book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. No Tzims, no interest. I'll just use my hombrew stuff to recreate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T10:25:36-08:00","id":1365293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1365277#post1365277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, my interest in it has dropped. Most of the rest of the book seem nice enough but not essential. Without the Ravnos and Tzimisce I do not see a need to buy the book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn\u2019t \u2018rewriting\u2019 imply that they are going to be in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T13:33:27-08:00","id":1365341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1365293#post1365293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn\u2019t \u2018rewriting\u2019 imply that they are going to be in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It does, it remains to be seen what that means, but given their insistence that the Convictions system can be used to mimick Paths, and that the sabbat will remain hidden, the interest I have in what exactly the Tzim will be is low, as Convictions cannot mimick paths, at all, the link to (extremely squicky and abusive forced relationships with) humans destroys that idea straight away (mostly because that premise gets a flat nope, it's way to close to the bone, and forcing people to play abusive stalkers is just not on, look at the degenerations linked to the Touchstones to see what I mean)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T13:53:04-08:00","id":1365342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1365277#post1365277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, my interest in it has dropped. Most of the rest of the book seem nice enough but not essential. Without the Ravnos and Tzimisce I do not see a need to buy the book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine they're going to be inside it.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I've heard they love the Tzimisce and want them to be perfect while Paradox actively hates the Ravnos for the reasons that they hate the Kuei-Jin. That's reddit hearsay and about as reliable as Twitter (which is to say not at all).<br /> <br /> I also don't know what they would want rewritten about the Tzimisce. Too gorey? Not gorey enough?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T15:50:26-08:00","id":1365382,"title":"","content":"What I most like about Tzimisce, and hope that is shown, is how they are macabre hosts, noble and ruthless, artists, scholars, sorcerers, ruffians, warriors, rebel rousers and delusional psychopaths all in the same clan. In a way it is a wicked brew of Ventrue, Brujah and Malkavian with devil pacts sprinkled into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T17:36:53-08:00","id":1365407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1365342#post1365342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine they're going to be inside it.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I've heard they love the Tzimisce and want them to be perfect while Paradox actively hates the Ravnos for the reasons that they hate the Kuei-Jin. That's reddit hearsay and about as reliable as Twitter (which is to say not at all).<br /> <br /> I also don't know what they would want rewritten about the Tzimisce. Too gorey? Not gorey enough?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most of that is online hearsay, yes. They're extrapolating from some of the devs from OPP talking about problematics with the Ravnos, as well as people who are no longer working for WW.<br /> <br /> As far as rewritten? I mean, they said it 'didn't fit WW's vision' in Dawkins' interview where he said Ravnos wouldn't be in and Tzimisce might not be. I would lay money on something being written outside of V5's design space, mechanical and thematic since 'as far as the Sabbat' was mentioned in relation to it. Probably wrote something that was 'really, this is only playable in the Sabbat' or somesuch and had it kicked back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 02-04-2020, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T19:19:06-08:00","id":1365428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1365291#post1365291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. No Tzims, no interest. I'll just use my hombrew stuff to recreate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I was a young man, I bought all the books and tried to follow the metaplot and rules closely. Now I buy only a few books and handwave everything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1365293#post1365293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn\u2019t \u2018rewriting\u2019 imply that they are going to be in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are more optimistic than I am.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T10:49:24-08:00","id":1432804,"title":"","content":"What will be of the Players Guide without adding the Salubri, Ravnos and Tzimisce?<br /> I love me some more options and alternate rules, specially in V5.<br /> But with the Companion out, what would be the big selling points of the Players Guide?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T17:22:02-08:00","id":1432861,"title":"","content":"Are they still making it? I had somewhat assumed that because of the delays the Companion was basically the best we were going to get.<br /> If they are though then I imagine consolidating all the clans into one book would be a big draw, introducing new types of Merits and Advantages, more Loresheets, and perhaps most interestingly new Discipline powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T17:45:15-08:00","id":1432865,"title":"","content":"I was left with the impression that the Player's Guide as we knew it was cancelled, and the Companion was what was salvaged from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T19:29:18-08:00","id":1432873,"title":"","content":"Well, I didn't get no info at all about cancellation or production difficulty (perhaps it could be rationalized from the fact of Covid is going on but...), and I do remember hearing about it in the last videos. Something like &quot;oh upcoming products...Sabbat guide book, Player Guide, Werewolf Apocalypse, yada-yada&quot;. So I'm assuming yes.<br /> What I would love to see is more useful systems like Response Algorithm (present in the Anarch book) that offers a base net of responses from a big individual or group to the actions of the coterie; Institutions simple attributes and rules for use (present in the Camarilla book) that makes it so that big groups, corporations, agencies and organizations can be represented mechanically. I find these very awesome, expanding the game and giving more tools that fill me up with ideas.<br /> <br /> But also, more Background options, more Loresheets (specially ones that are related to events, clans or ideas and can be used at more chronicles), more Merits and Flaws cuz the ones available are awesome but we need more, and the Coterie Merits (in the Companion) is a very cool idea. More Discipline power options would be nice but it could also unbalance the game or some such... so I'm not that interested.<br /> <br /> Other than that I think they will surprise us, for there really isn't much the game really needs right now, it's a very complete experience. So, more chronicles, lore or examples (of Touchstones, Convictions, types of coteries and predators) is mostly what I imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T23:43:30-08:00","id":1432888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1326877-v5-players-handbook-what-do-you-want-to-see?p=1432865#post1432865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was left with the impression that the Player's Guide as we knew it was cancelled, and the Companion was what was salvaged from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s how I read it too. What we know is that it hasn\u2019t been released by Modiphius, that there were some issues behind the scenes regarding how some canon details were to be developed, and that there has been a complete shift over in terms of the game\u2019s management moving forward, with an \u2018in house\u2019 development team now taking control. Some of the mooted content was included in the Companion, but I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if the release schedule is entirely different now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T06:59:03-08:00","id":1433046,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this press release suggests the PG is separate to the Companion: <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/en/world-of-darkness-names-renegade-game-studios-publishing-partner-for-its-catalogue-of-tabletop-rpgs/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/e...tabletop-rpgs/</a><br /> <br /> I can't find anything more recent, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}